# Bringing your own custom configuration
# The first line MUST match 00-common.config's first line so the workspaces CLI
# treats this as an additional drop-in that applies to all workspace hosts.
#
# Reverse-forwards the autoworker Slack broker. The broker runs on the laptop at
# 127.0.0.1:9077; this makes the SAME address reachable FROM the remote, tunneled
# back over the SSH connection. So on a workspace, `curl http://127.0.0.1:9077/...`
# hits the laptop-side broker. Binding to 127.0.0.1 (not 0.0.0.0) keeps it on the
# remote's loopback only — not exposed to the workspace network.
#
# The tunnel lives exactly as long as the SSH connection: close the laptop / drop
# the connection and the remote's autoworker falls back to its local spool until
# the tunnel returns. RemoteForward is additive, so this stacks with the
# workspaces daemon-socket forward in 00-common.config. We deliberately do NOT set
# ExitOnForwardFailure, so a forward hiccup never blocks the tmux session.
Match host "local-*,workspace-*,*.workspace.infra.dog"
    RemoteForward 127.0.0.1:9077 127.0.0.1:9077
